 "result": "**Mechanism:** a `ContextVar` plus werkzeug `LocalProxy` objects.\n\n- `src/tessel/globals.py:40` defines `_app_var = ContextVar(\"tessel.app_ctx\")`. It holds the current `AppContext`.\n- `src/tessel/globals.py:44-62` defines each global as a `LocalProxy` bound to `_app_var`. Each proxy reads the context var on every access and forwards to one attribute of the current `AppContext`:\n  - `active_app` → `ctx.app`\n  - `g` → `ctx.g`\n  - `request` → `ctx.request`\n  - `session` → `ctx.session`\n  - `app_ctx` → the context itself\n- `AppContext` is defined in `src/tessel/ctx.py:260`. `push()` (`ctx.py:416`, which calls `_app_var.set(self)` at line 433) makes it current. `pop()` (`ctx.py:446`, which calls `_app_var.reset(token)` at line 498) restores the previous one.\n- If no context is set, the proxy raises the \"Working outside of application/request context\" error. `request` and `session` use the request-specific message.\n\nBecause it is a `ContextVar`, each thread or async task sees its own context.",
